                  "content": "SELECTED: candidate_70\n\nCONFIDENCE: HIGH\n\nEXPLANATION:\nThe fix commit changes `int pageNum = 0;` to `int pageNum = -1;` inside the `getPageNumberFor(int index, int position)` method (by the time of the fix, this method lived in BookView.java). This initial value is the return value used to signal \"no valid page number\" / the title page, and initializing it to 0 instead of -1 caused the title page to incorrectly be reported as page number 0 (matching the fix commit message: \"Title-page has page-num 0 again\").\n\nTracing the history of this method across the candidates, `getPageNumberFor` first appears in candidate_70, where it is added as a brand-new method on `PageTurnerSpine.java`:\n\n```java\npublic int getPageNumberFor( int index, int position ) {\n    int pageNum = 0;\n    if ( index >= pageOffsets.size() ) {\n        return -1;\n    }\n    for ( int i=0; i < index; i++ ) {\n        pageNum += pageOffsets.get(i).size();\n    }\n    List<Integer> offsets = pageOffsets.get(index);\n    for ( int i=0; i < offsets.size() && offsets.get(i) < position; i++ ) {\n        pageNum++;\n    }\n    return pageNum;\n}\n```\n\nThis is the very first introduction of the `int pageNum = 0;` initialization that the fix later corrects to `-1`. All subsequent candidates that touch this method (candidate_80, 84, 104, 126, 147, 148, 157, 162, 163, 166) only refactor it (moving it into BookView.java, adding logging, adjusting the offset-comparison loop, adding a null-spine guard, etc.) but retain the same `pageNum = 0` initialization inherited from candidate_70. No candidate earlier than 70 contains this method at all (confirmed via search for \"getPageNumberFor\" and \"pageNum\" across all 173 candidate diffs), so candidate_70 is the commit that introduced the underlying off-by-one/initial-value bug that was eventually fixed.\n"
